   "description": "Khung môn học theo syllabus FLM chính thức.",
   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">CSI104 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.2</span>\n<h2>Grading: every mark and its weight</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Read this in week one — part of the grade is earned in class long before any exam.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 11210 · Decision 358/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 03/04/2024 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">CSI104 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.2</span>\n<h2>Cách tính điểm: đủ mọi đầu điểm và trọng số</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Đọc ngay tuần đầu — một phần điểm được tính trong lớp từ rất sớm, trước mọi kỳ thi.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 11210 · QĐ 358/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 03/04/2024 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Category<br><small>Đầu điểm</small></th><th>Type<br><small>Loại</small></th><th>Parts<br><small>Số phần</small></th><th>Weight<br><small>Trọng số</small></th><th>Completion criteria<br><small>Điều kiện hoàn thành</small></th><th>Duration<br><small>Thời lượng</small></th><th>CLO</th><th>Question type<br><small>Dạng câu hỏi</small></th><th>No. of questions<br><small>Số câu</small></th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>1</td><td><strong>Group presentation</strong></td><td>on-going</td><td>2</td><td><strong>10.0%</strong></td><td>&gt;0</td><td>Option 1: 30'/group Option 2 (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</td><td>LO1, LO2, LO3, LO4, LO5, LO6, LO7, LO8, LO9, LO10, LO11, LO12</td><td>Option 1: .ppt and oral presentation Option 2 (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</td><td>Option 1: N/A Option 2 (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td><strong>Lab</strong></td><td>on-going</td><td>2</td><td><strong>20.0%</strong></td><td>&gt;0</td><td>Option 1: 60-90'/each Option 2 (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</td><td></td><td>Option 1: practical exercises Option 2 (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</td><td>Option 1: N/A Option 2 (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td><strong>Progress test</strong></td><td>on-going</td><td>3</td><td><strong>30.0%</strong></td><td>&gt;0</td><td>Option 1: 30'/each Option 2 (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</td><td></td><td>Option 1: MC or suitable format Option 2 (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</td><td>Option 1: 30 Option 2 (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td><strong>Final exam</strong></td><td>Final exam</td><td>1</td><td><strong>40.0%</strong></td><td>4</td><td>60'</td><td></td><td>Multiple choicesMarked by Computer</td><td>60</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>The weights add up to <strong>100%</strong>. Minimum average to pass: <strong>5</strong>.</p>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\"><em>How to read \"Completion criteria\":</em> it is the minimum score that one mark must reach (e.g. <code>&gt;0</code> = you must not get zero / must sit it; <code>4</code> = at least 4/10). Missing it can mean failing the subject even with a good average — this reading is the website's explanation, the table itself is the university's.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>Tổng trọng số đúng <strong>100%</strong>. Điểm trung bình tối thiểu để qua môn: <strong>5</strong>.</p>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\"><em>Cách đọc cột \"Điều kiện hoàn thành\":</em> là điểm tối thiểu đầu điểm đó phải đạt (vd <code>&gt;0</code> = không được 0 / phải dự; <code>4</code> = tối thiểu 4/10). Không đạt có thể trượt môn dù điểm trung bình cao — phần giải thích này là của web, bảng là của trường.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>The fine print per mark (verbatim)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Group presentation</strong> — <em>Knowledge & skill:</em> one of the appendices.<br><em>Grading guide:</em> each group selects one topic to present at slot 6 &amp; slot 17 of syllabus; then prepares to present at slot 15 &amp; slot 22</li>\n<li><strong>Lab</strong> — <em>Knowledge & skill:</em> technical aspect of studied topics<br><em>Grading guide:</em> Guided by instructor<br><br>- Labs are arranged relevant to the chapter theory<br><br>- Student must finish labs and submit the results to the lecturer in class.</li>\n<li><strong>Progress test</strong> — <em>Knowledge & skill:</em> Test 1: Chaters 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 , 6 Test 2: Chapters 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 Test 3: Chapters 13, 14, 16, 20<br><em>Grading guide:</em> in class, by instructor<br><em>Note:</em> Instruction and schedules for Progress Tests must be presented in the Course Implementation Plan approved by director of the campus.<br><br>The test must be taken right after the last lectures of required material.<br><br>Instructor has responsibility to review the test for students after graded</li>\n<li><strong>Final exam</strong> — <em>Knowledge & skill:</em> concepts, algorithms; all studied Chapters<br><em>Grading guide:</em> by exam board,<br><br>using computer<br><em>Note:</em> The exam questions must be updated or different at least 70% to the previous ones.</li>\n</ul></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Chi tiết từng đầu điểm (nguyên văn)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Group presentation</strong> — <em>Kiến thức & kỹ năng:</em> one of the appendices.<br><em>Hướng dẫn chấm:</em> each group selects one topic to present at slot 6 &amp; slot 17 of syllabus; then prepares to present at slot 15 &amp; slot 22</li>\n<li><strong>Lab</strong> — <em>Kiến thức & kỹ năng:</em> technical aspect of studied topics<br><em>Hướng dẫn chấm:</em> Guided by instructor<br><br>- Labs are arranged relevant to the chapter theory<br><br>- Student must finish labs and submit the results to the lecturer in class.</li>\n<li><strong>Progress test</strong> — <em>Kiến thức & kỹ năng:</em> Test 1: Chaters 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 , 6 Test 2: Chapters 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 Test 3: Chapters 13, 14, 16, 20<br><em>Hướng dẫn chấm:</em> in class, by instructor<br><em>Ghi chú:</em> Instruction and schedules for Progress Tests must be presented in the Course Implementation Plan approved by director of the campus.<br><br>The test must be taken right after the last lectures of required material.<br><br>Instructor has responsibility to review the test for students after graded</li>\n<li><strong>Final exam</strong> — <em>Kiến thức & kỹ năng:</em> concepts, algorithms; all studied Chapters<br><em>Hướng dẫn chấm:</em> by exam board,<br><br>using computer<br><em>Ghi chú:</em> The exam questions must be updated or different at least 70% to the previous ones.</li>\n</ul></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=11210\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=11210</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=11210\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=11210</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
